WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.525
Imagine opening a notice about support at home

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.865
and still not knowing what to do next.

3
00:00:06.883 --> 00:00:09.403
A team wants clearer information about Community First Services

4
00:00:09.423 --> 00:00:12.283
and Supports, or C F S S.

5
00:00:13.317 --> 00:00:14.392
Let's turn that intention

6
00:00:14.427 --> 00:00:16.607
into a useful working draft.

7
00:00:16.807 --> 00:00:18.952
We are using the practice workspace accompanying

8
00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:21.752
the DHS Equity Analysis Toolkit training.

9
00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.872
Its five fields help organize thinking.

10
00:00:23.907 --> 00:00:25.632
They are not the official toolkit sequence, and

11
00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.252
filling them in does not complete a required

12
00:00:27.287 --> 00:00:28.687
review.

13
00:00:31.137 --> 00:00:33.422
In The decision and its limits, writing make

14
00:00:33.457 --> 00:00:36.002
the notice equitable gives us an intention, but

15
00:00:36.037 --> 00:00:38.802
no decision to examine. Instead, describe the

16
00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:41.017
choices that are actually open.

17
00:00:41.217 --> 00:00:44.402
Our draft says: revise the explanation, format,

18
00:00:44.437 --> 00:00:46.462
and route to help, so readers can identify

19
00:00:46.497 --> 00:00:49.222
their next step. Confirm current guidance and

20
00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:51.282
who can authorize these changes.

21
00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.262
Eligibility rules are outside this notice

22
00:00:53.297 --> 00:00:55.582
revision. That separates communication choices

23
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:58.297
from decisions the team cannot make.

24
00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:06.802
In People, evidence, and unanswered questions,

25
00:01:06.837 --> 00:01:08.762
everyone benefits is too broad.

26
00:01:08.797 --> 00:01:10.642
It conceals differences in who can read,

27
00:01:10.677 --> 00:01:13.442
understand, and act. An English-only document or

28
00:01:13.477 --> 00:01:15.762
an online-only response can transfer extra work

29
00:01:15.797 --> 00:01:18.197
to people already facing barriers.

30
00:01:18.397 --> 00:01:20.802
Our draft asks about language and disability

31
00:01:20.837 --> 00:01:24.142
access, shared devices, and getting assistance.

32
00:01:24.177 --> 00:01:25.762
Review available questions and usability

33
00:01:25.797 --> 00:01:28.962
evidence; seek missing perspectives directly.

34
00:01:28.997 --> 00:01:30.942
We have not established what people need.

35
00:01:30.977 --> 00:01:32.982
Do not infer a person's preferences from their

36
00:01:33.017 --> 00:01:35.637
race, language, or disability.

37
00:01:41.337 --> 00:01:43.782
In Options and tradeoffs, translate it is a

38
00:01:43.817 --> 00:01:46.062
possible action, not a comparison.

39
00:01:46.097 --> 00:01:48.362
Consider keeping the existing notice, revising a

40
00:01:48.397 --> 00:01:50.522
paper explanation, or offering accessible

41
00:01:50.557 --> 00:01:53.297
formats and a supported route to help.

42
00:01:53.497 --> 00:01:56.202
Paper can reduce dependence on internet access,

43
00:01:56.237 --> 00:01:58.222
but paper alone will not meet every language

44
00:01:58.257 --> 00:02:00.762
or disability access need. More formats may

45
00:02:00.797 --> 00:02:03.622
improve access, but require review, staff time,

46
00:02:03.657 --> 00:02:06.017
and a way to keep each version current.

47
00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:08.222
Record who could benefit, who could carry

48
00:02:08.257 --> 00:02:11.302
additional burdens, and what remains uncertain.

49
00:02:11.337 --> 00:02:12.842
Use the plain-language and language-access

50
00:02:12.877 --> 00:02:15.602
resources to identify adjustments, then test

51
00:02:15.637 --> 00:02:17.562
them with affected people rather than assuming

52
00:02:17.597 --> 00:02:19.857
the proposed solution works.

53
00:02:25.557 --> 00:02:28.422
In Participation and next actions, ask the

54
00:02:28.457 --> 00:02:30.262
community leaves power and responsibility

55
00:02:30.297 --> 00:02:33.382
unclear. Invite people who use services while

56
00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:35.542
the wording, formats, and help route can still

57
00:02:35.577 --> 00:02:37.982
change. Offer ways to participate that fit

58
00:02:38.017 --> 00:02:41.037
people's language, access, and scheduling needs.

59
00:02:41.237 --> 00:02:43.482
Our draft assigns a communications lead to

60
00:02:43.517 --> 00:02:45.522
coordinate review and report back on what

61
00:02:45.557 --> 00:02:47.902
changed, what did not, and why.

62
00:02:47.937 --> 00:02:49.602
Confirm decision authority, participation

63
00:02:49.637 --> 00:02:52.582
supports, and resources. One meeting or one

64
00:02:52.617 --> 00:02:54.482
person cannot establish agreement for every

65
00:02:54.517 --> 00:02:55.837
community.

66
00:03:01.537 --> 00:03:04.422
In Review responsibilities and reconsideration,

67
00:03:04.457 --> 00:03:06.942
count notices sent measures distribution.

68
00:03:06.977 --> 00:03:08.602
It does not tell us whether people understood

69
00:03:08.637 --> 00:03:11.302
or could act. Ask readers to describe their

70
00:03:11.337 --> 00:03:13.402
next step and examine unanswered questions,

71
00:03:13.437 --> 00:03:16.297
assistance requests, and people not reached.

72
00:03:16.497 --> 00:03:19.342
Name who will review that information, agree a

73
00:03:19.377 --> 00:03:21.302
review date, and identify a reason to

74
00:03:21.337 --> 00:03:23.682
reconsider. For example, repeated confusion

75
00:03:23.717 --> 00:03:25.422
about where to get help would prompt another

76
00:03:25.457 --> 00:03:28.082
revision. Assign responsibility and resources

77
00:03:28.117 --> 00:03:30.082
for maintaining every format as guidance

78
00:03:30.117 --> 00:03:31.417
changes.

79
00:03:37.117 --> 00:03:39.462
Together, these notes can inform an equity

80
00:03:39.497 --> 00:03:41.962
impact statement: the proposed changes may

81
00:03:41.997 --> 00:03:44.402
reduce communication barriers, but evidence and

82
00:03:44.437 --> 00:03:46.802
engagement are still needed. The training also

83
00:03:46.837 --> 00:03:49.262
addresses alignment and sustainability. Check

84
00:03:49.297 --> 00:03:51.442
that recommendations fit current guidance and

85
00:03:51.477 --> 00:03:53.477
can be supported over time.

86
00:03:55.927 --> 00:03:58.112
Now try a different decision in the existing

87
00:03:58.147 --> 00:03:58.727
workspace.

88
00:03:59.217 --> 00:04:02.517
A service team is considering replacing mailed appointment reminders

89
00:04:02.537 --> 00:04:03.237
with texts.

90
00:04:04.217 --> 00:04:05.572
Work through its example,

91
00:04:05.607 --> 00:04:07.252
then use the five draft fields to prepare

92
00:04:07.287 --> 00:04:09.327
your own analysis.

93
00:04:09.527 --> 00:04:11.652
Describe what can change, whose experience is

94
00:04:11.687 --> 00:04:14.312
missing, two workable options, how people can

95
00:04:14.347 --> 00:04:16.972
influence the decision, and when to revisit it.

96
00:04:17.007 --> 00:04:18.992
Explain one tradeoff rather than copying our

97
00:04:19.027 --> 00:04:21.552
notice example. Keep practice notes separate

98
00:04:21.587 --> 00:04:24.172
from actual work and exclude identifying or

99
00:04:24.207 --> 00:04:26.047
confidential details.

100
00:04:28.717 --> 00:04:31.517
Choose Save to My Work and check the confirmation

101
00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:34.897
before leaving. Your notes stay in this browser on

102
00:04:34.917 --> 00:04:37.777
this device after you save them. You can also

103
00:04:37.797 --> 00:04:41.197
download or print them. Unsaved changes can be lost

104
00:04:41.217 --> 00:04:42.577
